1️⃣ Step 1 — Create Groups
Groups represent departments/permissions.
# System groups
sudo groupadd devops
sudo groupadd backend
sudo groupadd frontend
sudo groupadd qa
sudo groupadd security
sudo groupadd finance



Each group controls access to directories, scripts, or servers.


Admin/root group is already root.



2️⃣ Step 2 — Create Users and Assign to Groups
# DevOps users
sudo useradd -m -G devops,sudo devops1
sudo useradd -m -G devops,sudo devops2

# Backend users
sudo useradd -m -G backend backend1
sudo useradd -m -G backend backend2

# Frontend
sudo useradd -m -G frontend frontend1

# QA
sudo useradd -m -G qa qa1

# Security
sudo useradd -m -G security,sudo sec1

# Finance
sudo useradd -m -G finance finance1

Notes:


Only DevOps and Security get sudo access.


Other groups have limited access — principle of least privilege.



3️⃣ Step 3 — Set Directory Structure & Permissions
Simulate shared directories per department:
# Shared application directory
sudo mkdir -p /apps/backend
sudo mkdir -p /apps/frontend
sudo mkdir -p /staging
sudo mkdir -p /shared/infra
sudo mkdir -p /finance/reports


Set Group Ownership
sudo chown root:backend /apps/backend
sudo chown root:frontend /apps/frontend
sudo chown root:qa /staging
sudo chown root:devops /shared/infra
sudo chown root:finance /finance/reports


Set Permissions


Owner (root) → full control


Group → read/write/execute if needed


Others → no access


sudo chmod 770 /apps/backend
sudo chmod 770 /apps/frontend
sudo chmod 770 /staging
sudo chmod 770 /shared/infra
sudo chmod 770 /finance/reports

✅ This ensures:


DevOps can deploy in /shared/infra


Backend team can only access backend app


QA can access staging


Finance can only access reports


No random user can access critical directories



4️⃣ Step 4 — Configure Sudo Access
Granular sudo for DevOps and Security


Open sudoers safely:


sudo visudo



Add user-specific or group-specific rules:


# DevOps can run all admin tasks
%devops ALL=(ALL) ALL

# Security can audit logs
%security ALL=(ALL) /usr/bin/journalctl, /usr/bin/less /var/log/*

# Backend/frontend/QA/Finance -> no sudo


5️⃣ Step 5 — Optional: Restrict su


Only allow security and devops users to switch users:


# Add PAM restriction in /etc/pam.d/su
auth       required   pam_wheel.so use_uid group=sudo



Only users in sudo group can su to root.


Normal engineers cannot switch users.



6️⃣ Step 6 — Audit & Logging


All sudo commands logged: /var/log/auth.log


Security group monitors logs daily.


sudo tail -f /var/log/auth.log



Set home directory isolation:


chmod 700 /home/devops1
chmod 700 /home/backend1



Prevents other users from reading personal configs.



